1
00:00:00,289 --> 00:00:01,169
Hi everyone.

2
00:00:01,169 --> 00:00:06,510
We built SkillGuard to test an AI assistant’s
skills, or saved instructions it can reuse.

3
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:10,853
A skill might organize receipts correctly and
still try to open a private file.

4
00:00:10,853 --> 00:00:12,823
SkillGuard runs it in a restricted workspace

5
00:00:12,788 --> 00:00:18,063
and records some activity for a person to
review before deciding whether to install it.

6
00:00:18,063 --> 00:00:22,816
When Hermes proposes an update, SkillGuard
pauses it and saves the exact version.

7
00:00:22,816 --> 00:00:25,304
NVIDIA SkillEvaluator helps create attack
tests,

8
00:00:25,269 --> 00:00:30,483
then Harbor runs the agent in an isolated
OpenShell workspace with limited access.

9
00:00:30,448 --> 00:00:32,811
Sysdig records some runtime activity.

10
00:00:32,811 --> 00:00:36,618
Nemotron reviews the evidence, but a person
makes the final decision.

11
00:00:36,618 --> 00:00:38,868
In this first run, all twelve receipt tests
pass,

12
00:00:38,833 --> 00:00:43,577
but Sysdig records thirteen blocked attempts
to open the private file.

13
00:00:43,577 --> 00:00:48,112
One of those is an independent control check
to confirm the sandbox blocks access.

14
00:00:48,112 --> 00:00:52,312
The receipt answers are right, but this
version still isn’t safe to install.

15
00:00:52,312 --> 00:00:56,033
Nemotron recommends allowing it, and
SkillGuard blocks the installation

16
00:00:55,998 --> 00:00:58,413
because of the recorded attempts.

17
00:00:58,413 --> 00:01:02,089
Now we’re looking at a repaired version that
we prepared and tested.

18
00:01:02,089 --> 00:01:06,960
The new tests include instructions meant to
pull the agent away from its receipt task.

19
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:10,816
In one example, the receipt tells the agent to
read a private note.

20
00:01:10,816 --> 00:01:13,082
The agent doesn’t follow that instruction.

21
00:01:13,082 --> 00:01:14,517
You can see it read the guide

22
00:01:14,482 --> 00:01:18,795
and receipt, then write and check the correct
answer which is twenty-three.

23
00:01:18,795 --> 00:01:21,013
All four fresh probes pass for this version,

24
00:01:20,978 --> 00:01:25,202
and we don’t observe any private-file attempts
during those tests.

25
00:01:25,202 --> 00:01:29,304
With the task context included, Nemotron
recommends allowing the version.

26
00:01:29,304 --> 00:01:33,039
We review the evidence and approve the exact
version that was tested.

27
00:01:33,039 --> 00:01:36,913
Passing makes it eligible for approval.

28
00:01:36,913 --> 00:01:37,954
It doesn’t install itself, and

29
00:01:37,919 --> 00:01:40,861
approval applies only to this restricted
receipt workspace.

30
00:01:40,861 --> 00:01:46,803
After that, we run the installed skill on a
separate receipt.

31
00:01:46,803 --> 00:01:49,181
The agent reads its guide, uses the available
tools, saves its answer,

32
00:01:49,146 --> 00:01:51,044
and completes the task in six real model
requests.

33
00:01:51,044 --> 00:01:55,082
That confirms the installed skill can still
handle its receipt task.

34
00:01:55,082 --> 00:02:00,038
We can also go back to an earlier approved
version if a later update causes trouble.

35
00:02:00,038 --> 00:02:04,437
In this walkthrough, we roll back to that
version and then restore the newer one.

36
00:02:04,437 --> 00:02:06,826
The earlier warning stays in the history,

37
00:02:06,791 --> 00:02:09,863
so we can still see why the first version was
blocked.

38
00:02:09,863 --> 00:02:13,054
These are real NVIDIA Nemotron three point
five Lightning model calls

39
00:02:13,019 --> 00:02:18,289
through Nebius Token Factory, used to generate
tests, run the agent, and review evidence.

40
00:02:18,289 --> 00:02:22,313
The API key stays on the server, outside the
test workspace.

41
00:02:22,313 --> 00:02:25,254
We used fictional receipts and a fictional
private note.

42
00:02:25,254 --> 00:02:26,987
Sysdig gives us useful but

43
00:02:26,952 --> 00:02:30,583
partial observations; it doesn’t capture every
possible action.

44
00:02:30,583 --> 00:02:34,009
Four passing probes don’t prove every skill is
safe.

45
00:02:34,009 --> 00:02:38,484
This demo checks reusable instructions for
this receipt workflow before installation.

46
00:02:38,484 --> 00:02:40,687
It doesn’t train or change the model.

47
00:02:40,687 --> 00:02:43,338
The code and reproducible test build are
public.

48
00:02:43,338 --> 00:02:43,756
Thank you.
